Figure 3 illustrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response and is taken up by recruited immune cells at the injection site. Panel A shows the kinetics of various inflammatory cell types, revealing a rapid increase in Mac-2+ macrophages and Ly6C+ monocytes that peaks around day 2, while neutrophils are transiently present at 6 hours post-injection. Panel B provides confocal microscopy images, demonstrating the intracellular presence of Nano-11 within MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages at different time points, confirming its efficient phagocytosis by these cells at the injection site.